    <string name="accessibility_service_label">Open Android Use Companion</string>
    <string name="accessibility_service_description">Lets the Open Android Use agent see the screen and perform UI actions on your behalf. The control endpoint listens on this device only (127.0.0.1) and is reachable from a computer solely through USB debugging. Disable this service at any time to cut the agent off.</string>

    <string name="restricted_setting_hint">On Android 13+, if you sideloaded this app you may see a “Restricted setting” notice when enabling accessibility. To allow it: open Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Open Android Use Companion, tap the ⋮ menu (top-right), choose “Allow restricted settings,” then return and enable the service. (This step goes away when the app is installed from the Play Store.)</string>

